GitHub Security Lab advisory GHSL-2025-121_GHSL-2025-123: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), Unvalidated Redirect, and Extensive Remote Proxy Capabilities in NocoDB - CVE-2026-24769, CVE-2026-24768, CVE-2026-53931 (March 12, 2026)
Coordinated Disclosure Timeline
2025-11-26: Vulnerabilities were reported via GitHub’s private vulnerability reporting feature.
2026-01-28: GHSL-2025-121 + GHSL-2025-122 were fixed.
Summary
NocoDB version 0.265.1 contains multiple vulnerabilities, including a stored cross-site scripting (GHSL-2025-121), an unvalidated redirect in the login mechanism (GHSL-2025-122), and extensive remote proxy capabilities through an unauthenticated endpoint (GHSL-2025-123).
Project
nocodb
Tested Version
v0.265.1
Details
Issue 1: Stored Cross-Site Scripting via SVG upload ( GHSL-2025-121 )
A stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability was found in NocoDB’s attachment handling mechanism that allows authenticated users to upload malicious SVG files containing JavaScript code. When these files are viewed by other users, the embedded scripts execute in the victim’s browser context, enabling account compromise, data exfiltration, and privilege escalation.
Root Cause: NocoDB treats any file with a mime type containing the substring 'image' as safe for inline preview without content sanitization. SVG files ( image/svg+xml ) can contain executable JavaScript via <script> tags, event handlers, or external references. The application serves uploaded SVG files with Content-Disposition: inline and their original Content-Type: image/svg+xml , causing browsers to render and execute embedded scripts under the application’s origin.
This is due to:
An overly permissive previewable MIME type check in attachmentHelpers.ts
const previewableMimeTypes = [ ' image ' , ' pdf ' , ' video ' , ' audio ' ];
export const isPreviewAllowed = ( args : { mimetype ?: string } = {}) => {
const { mimetype } = args ;
if ( ! mimetype ) return false ;
return previewableMimeTypes . some (( type ) => mimetype . includes ( type ));
};
This function uses substring matching ( includes ), causing image/svg+xml to be classified as previewable despite SVG files being able to contain executable code. Afterwards the file’s MIME type is preserved without validation or sanitization, allowing image/svg+xml to pass through unchanged.
The file being served without sanitization in the attachments.controller.ts (fileReadv3 endpoint)
@ Get ( ' /dltemp/:param(*) ' )
async fileReadv3 (@ Param ( ' param ' ) param : string , @ Res () res : Response ) {
// No authentication guard
// Retrieves signed URL parameters including Content-Type and Content-Disposition
// Lines 194-205: Sets headers from query parameters
res . setHeader ( ' Content-Type ' , queryParams . contentType );
res . setHeader ( ' Content-Disposition ' , queryParams . contentDisposition );
// Line 213: Sends raw file content
res . sendFile ( file . path );
}
Impact
This issue may lead to account takeover due to stored Cross-site scripting (XSS).
CWEs
CWE-79 : Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation (‘Cross-site Scripting’)
CWE-434 : Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type
Issue 2: Unvalidated Redirect in Login ( GHSL-2025-122 )
An unvalidated redirect vulnerability exists in NocoDB’s login functionality.
In NocoDB’s redirect functionality :
Lines 1-3: isFullUrl regex /^(https?:)?\/\// accepts any HTTP(S) or protocol-relative URL
Lines 32-40: Unconditional external navigation when continueAfterSignIn matches the regex:
navigateTo ( route . value . query . continueAfterSignIn as string , {
external : isFullUrl (...)
})
No validation of domain, origin, or protocol restrictions
Proof of Concept
Attacker crafts malicious link: https://victim-nocodb.example/#/signin?continueAfterSignIn=https://evil-phishing.com/fake-login
Victim clicks link (via email, social engineering, etc.) and sees legitimate NocoDB sign-in page
Victim authenticates with valid credentials
NocoDB redirects to attacker’s site:
Attacker’s site displays a Login form and says the Login failed.
Victim re-enter credentials into attacker’s site.
Impact
This vulnerability could be used by attackers in phishing attacks by tricking victims into re-entering their credentials in a malicious site.
CWEs
CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site (‘Open Redirect’)
Issue 3: Extensive Remote Proxy Capabilities in Unauthenticated Endpoint ( GHSL-2025-123 )
